  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "CUBEVALUE sums <=6-decimal columns as exact scaled integers, returns 1 without a measure, returns \"\" on empty slices, and rejects duplicate hierarchies with #VALUE!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, CUBEVALUE(connection, [member_expression1], ...) evaluates SUM over a workbook data model column whose entries all have at most 6 decimal places as an exact scaled integer rounded once to binary64 (returning 42.3, 0x4045266666666666, for {10, 20, 5, 7, 0.1, 0.2}, whereas binary64 row-order addition gives 42.300000000000004). With members and no measure it returns 1; with an empty slice it returns \"\"; when given a CUBESET it sums across the set's members; two members from one hierarchy or two measures return #VALUE!; and numbers or \"\" return #N/A. All 4,246 full-bank CUBEVALUE rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/cube/measured.xlsx and pivot_cube/oracle.xlsx (Excel 16.0.20527); 4,246/4,246 full-bank rows match.",
